    {
      "id": "CLM-01",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-class-slabs-line",
      "title": "The total mass of the rank-one determinant slabs",
      "statement": "For a totally complex number field E with f conjugate pairs, the sum over the rank-one coefficient-lattice classes is πᶠhR/w, equivalently the residue of ζ_E at one times the Euclidean covolume of its integer ring.",
      "hypotheses": "Full lattices up to a rational change of basis, ordinary complex area at every place, and one unit of logarithmic determinant width. The regulator uses doubled logarithms at complex places.",
